  "notes": "Jodeci's producer and the Swing Mob's founder — raw, church-derived Uptown R&B, windowed **1990–1996** by the research. The band is \"56–70 half-time (backbeat on beat 3) plus 86–93 straight\", so the felt band is the base with the mode at 61 and F minor as the named house key across three albums. Three drum deltas: \"kick on 1 plus the 8th before 3\" at one or two hits with syncopation 0.08 and a 0.15 `beatSkipProb`, \"clap/snare on beat 3 only\" with the clap pushed 4–10 ms behind a snare that is itself 4–11 ms late, and \"almost no hat lane; where hats appear they are low-velocity 16ths\" at 0.07 fill density. The distinguishing claim is that the rawness is a **mix** decision, not just a programming one — \"he also engineered and mixed… so the rawness is a mix decision as much as a programming one\" — which is encoded as a deliberately low `velocityTiers` set (104–120 accent over a 62–80 main), a 0.62 quantize and a −12 dB perc bed; nothing else in this section is mixed this far down on purpose. Harmony is \"gospel-quartet voicing — m7, m9 and sus4 resolutions, two- and four-bar vamps carried by organ or Rhodes **with no countermelody**\", so `susSubstitutionProb` is 0.5 — the highest in the section — ninth is 0.38, and the counter is pushed to a 0.16 pad rather than deleted. \"The arrangement leaves space for full-throat melisma\" is the wide melody register, the low chord-tone bias and the highest leap share among the ballad producers. The bass is \"long-sustaining synth bass holding the root for a whole bar, **sitting above true sub territory** and mixed loud\" — hence a register floor of MIDI 30 rather than the 24 the 808 models use. ⚠ The machine lineage is `[LOW-CONF]` in the research and has no schema field. ⚠ Every velocity and density number is INFERRED.",
